  "design": {
    "entrance": "A soft, swollen, dull-red billet in the rough shape of the title heats up in the dark; three hammer strikes (left, right, centre) each flatten it, sharpen the edges and throw sparks.",
    "reveal": "The final strike on the impact frame locks the crisp forged title at white-orange heat; glowing seams pulse, then the metal cools in a controlled way to dark hammered iron with ember-red seams.",
    "camera": "Static, heavy framing with a hard jolt on every strike and a slow creep-in during cooling.",
    "material": "Hammered dark iron (concrete-grain bump, flat chamfer) with emissive heat driven by a blackbody ramp; edge and crack seams stay hot longest; forge underlight from below.",
    "exit": "The last heat drains from the seams and quench steam rolls over the cold iron until it is gone."
  },
